# Copy to `.env` before running anything.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run db:up` starts a Postgres on your machine with no Docker and
# nothing to install, and prints a connection string. The default below
# matches what it hands out.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:51214/viemo?sslmode=disable"

# ── Deployed ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any Postgres works. Supabase gives the pooled connection string under
# Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI:
#
#   DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"
#
# Never commit a real connection string. `.env` is gitignored; this file
# is the only one that ships.

# ── Cookies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave unset anywhere with HTTPS. Set to false only on a host that can
# only serve over HTTP — a Secure cookie is never returned over HTTP, and
# the symptom is a sign-in that appears to work and then bounces straight
# back. See lib/auth/session.ts.
# COOKIE_SECURE=false
